0..77 Comment "//! Temporary access. `var c = e;` keeps a value for the rest of a block, and"
78..159 Comment "//! `access c as v { … }` lends it to the view `v`, which the body ends exactly"
160..237 Comment "//! once: `resume v e` writes `e` back, `abort v` leaves the held value as it"
238..318 Comment "//! was and runs the access\'s `unwind` clause instead. The unwind runs under the"
319..392 Comment "//! empty row, and an access with none unwinds by doing nothing. The loan"
393..466 Comment "//! follows Rust\'s mutable borrow, ended once [Rust-reference], § Borrow"
467..481 Comment "//! operators."
482..485 Comment "//!"
486..515 Comment "//! - cites: [Rust-reference]"
516..519 Comment "//!"
520..617 Comment "//! [Rust-reference]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/ \"The Rust Project, The Rust Reference\""
619..695 Comment "/// The successor, a call whose type synthesises where a statement binds it."
